Build TripPilot AI, a responsive, production-quality, AI-native travel planning, booking, live-safety, and intelligent replanning web app in Google AI Studio.

TripPilot AI should feel like a premium travel marketplace such as MakeMyTrip, but powered by an autonomous AI travel agent that can plan personalized trips, compare and book packages, monitor a journey in real time, detect risks, translate languages, manage group decisions, control budget, and automatically replan when disruptions occur.

Use React, Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion, React Three Fiber, @react-three/drei, Lucide React, Zustand, React Router, Recharts, and the Gemini API.

Use realistic mock data for flights, trains, buses, hotels, packages, weather, traffic, hospitals, police stations, road risk, fuel stops, expenses, attractions, and local food so the complete demo works without paid travel APIs.

Do not hardcode API keys. Read Gemini and Google Maps credentials from environment variables or AI Studio’s Secrets panel. Prefer server-side/API-route Gemini calls so keys are never exposed in the browser; if Gemini fails, is rate-limited, or unavailable, gracefully fall back to realistic hardcoded demo data and display a small “Demo data” badge.

Core Product Vision
TripPilot AI is a 6-step guided travel operating system:

Plan — AI understands the traveler’s intent and creates a personalized itinerary.

Package — AI compares transport, stay, meals, activities, and cancellation options.

Verify & Book — Traveler details, validation, mock payment, and booking confirmation.

Companion — Live dashboard during the trip: navigation, safety, weather, expenses, translation, and alerts.

Replan — AI detects disruptions and proposes safe, budget-aware alternatives.

Dossier — Downloadable/shareable smart trip document with itinerary, bookings, contacts, emergency info, and expenses.

The app must support global destinations, India-first travel intelligence, deep Tamil Nadu coverage, full multilingual UI, Trip Mode personalization, offline emergency access, and a persistent AI assistant.

